Have you tried turning colour on?  You'll still have to learn the new
symbols, but it makes it a lot easier to distinguish between the various
members of each class than mono.  Now I only need the / command on a few
occasions:

purple h (dwarf king/(master) mind flayer)
dark blue D (black/blue dragon)
white f/d (how big's that domestic animal?)
purple @ (Rodney/Elvenking)
purple & (riders, and summoned named daemons)
white @ (mainly to tell whether it's peaceful/coaligned)

>  and net delay

I find the delay makes me play more carefully - if I'm doing anything
remotely tricky, I wait for the display to react before making another
move.  I've also found that typing "9s" is a much better way of making
that hidden door appear than just leaning on the "s" key for a while.

